## 4. The Governed GitOps Lifecycle

In an enterprise environment, developers do not manually create Bitrise apps by clicking through web forms. Instead, all enrollment is governed through **GitOps**:

```
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                           GITOPS ENROLLMENT FLOW                              |
|                                                                               |
|  [Developer Repo]              [Config Repo: develop]     [Config Repo: main] |
|   Write source code     --->    Submit secret-free    ---> Reviewed promotion |
|   Ready for enrollment          app.yaml request           to main branch     |
|                                                                  |            |
|                                                                  v            |
|                                                        Bitrise App Created    |
|                                                        Once via Automation    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### 4.1 One-Time Enrollment vs. Later Builds

* **One-Time Enrollment**: Initial enrollment creates the Bitrise project **once**. A developer submits a secret-free YAML request file (<code>config/teams/&lt;team&gt;/bitrise/apps/&lt;app&gt;.yaml</code>) to the platform configuration repository. Once reviewed and merged to <code>main</code>, automation calls the Bitrise API to initialize the app, attach approved workflow templates, and link protected signing keys.
* **Later Builds**: Subsequent releases reuse the existing Bitrise project. Recurring builds trigger automatically on code pushes and Pull Requests. Developers never re-submit enrollment requests for existing apps.

### 4.2 The Secret-Free Request YAML Contract

The enrollment file contains zero credentials or signing data:

```yaml
app_name: my-mobile-app
team: mobile-platform
repo_url: https://git.enterprise.internal/mobile-engineering/my-mobile-app.git
source_branch: development
platform: react-native
template_id: react-native-standard
template_version: 1.15.9
access_groups:
  - Mobile_Engineering
optional_users: []
```

#### Strict Contract Rules:
1. **Filename Identity**: The file must reside at <code>config/teams/&lt;team&gt;/bitrise/apps/&lt;app&gt;.yaml</code>. The folder name must equal <code>team</code>; the filename must equal <code>app_name</code>.
2. **Create-Only Policy**: The contract is strictly create-only. Actions like <code>action: update</code>, <code>operation: reconcile</code>, or <code>delete: true</code> are rejected by pre-merge validators.
3. **Zero Secret Boundary**: The inclusion of tokens, passwords, private keys, or keystores will trigger immediate validation rejection.

