## 6. The 7-Stage Evidence &amp; Verification Ladder

In an enterprise release audit, an application is never certified as "released" simply because a build completed. The delivery pipeline must establish proof across seven sequential checkpoints:

<DiagramExpand title="THE 7-STAGE EVIDENCE &amp; VERIFICATION LADDER">

```mermaid
graph TD
    S1["1. BuildStarted<br/>Exact branch, commit hash, and workflow ID confirmed"] --> S2["2. BuildSuccessful<br/>Zero compilation errors on clean Bitrise virtual machine"]
    S2 --> S3["3. ArtifactValidated<br/>File size > 0 &bull; SHA-256 integrity hash matches"]
    S3 --> S4["4. Uploaded<br/>Readback verifies binary received by distribution platform"]
    S4 --> S5["5. Signed<br/>Verified cryptographic signature using enterprise release credential"]
    S5 --> S6["6. Enabled<br/>Exact signed version toggled active in enterprise catalog"]
    S6 --> S7["7. Assigned &amp; UserVisible<br/>Assigned to 'All Users' &amp; endpoint returns latest version"]
```

</DiagramExpand>

