## 4. Step 3: GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT) Setup

Danger requires GitHub API access to read PR metadata and post comments on your pull requests.

### 4.1 Creating the Personal Access Token in GitHub

1. Log into your GitHub Enterprise account.
2. In the top right corner, click your profile picture &gt; **Settings**.
3. In the left navigation, scroll to the bottom and click **Developer settings**.
4. Click **Personal access tokens** &gt; **Tokens (classic)**.
5. Click **Generate new token (classic)**.
6. Set **Note** to: <code>Bitrise-Danger-Bot</code>.
7. Under **Select scopes**, check the **repo** scope (Full control of private repositories).
8. Click **Generate token** and copy the resulting string (e.g., <code>ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxx</code>).

### 4.2 Storing the Token in Bitrise Secrets

1. Open your mobile application in the **Bitrise Console**.
2. Click **Workflow Editor** &gt; **Secrets Tab**.
3. Add a new secret:
   * **Key**: <code>DANGER_GITHUB_API_TOKEN</code>
   * **Value**: <code>ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxx</code>
4. For GitHub Enterprise installations, also declare these environment variables in your <code>app.envs</code>:
   * <code>DANGER_GITHUB_HOST</code>: <code>git.enterprise.internal</code>
   * <code>DANGER_GITHUB_API_BASE_URL</code>: <code>https://git.enterprise.internal/api/v3</code>

