## 5. Step 4: Connecting the Release Pipeline

Once your secrets and signing keys are registered, the <code>release-prod</code> workflow connects them directly into build steps:

<div class="portal-code-frame">
  <div class="portal-code-header">
    <span class="portal-file-badge">bitrise.yml (release-prod excerpt)</span>
    <span class="portal-badge-hub">HEADLESS CODE SIGNING</span>
  </div>
  <pre class="portal-code-block"><code>workflows:
  release-prod:
    steps:
    # 1. Compile &amp; Sign Android Production AAB
    - android-build@1:
        title: Build Production Android App Bundle (.aab)
        inputs:
        - project_location: $PROJECT_LOCATION
        - module: $MODULE
        - variant: prodRelease
        - build_type: aab
    - sign-apk@1: {}

    # 2. Archive &amp; Sign iOS Production IPA with Apple API Key
    - xcode-archive@5:
        title: Archive Production iOS IPA
        inputs:
        - project_path: $BITRISE_PROJECT_PATH
        - scheme: $BITRISE_SCHEME
        - distribution_method: app-store
        - automatic_code_signing: api-key

    # 3. Deliver to Apple TestFlight
    - deploy-to-itunesconnect-with-deliver@3:
        inputs:
        - api_key_url: $APP_STORE_CONNECT_API_KEY_URL
        - api_issuer_id: $APP_STORE_CONNECT_ISSUER_ID
        - api_key_id: $APP_STORE_CONNECT_KEY_ID
        - ipa_path: $BITRISE_IPA_PATH
        - submit_for_review: "no"</code></pre>
</div>

