## 1. Why Real-Device Cloud Testing Matters

Simulators and emulators on developer laptops cannot accurately replicate physical device realities:
* **OEM Customizations**: Samsung One UI, Xiaomi MIUI, and Google Pixel skins alter background task execution and push notifications.
* **Hardware Sensors &amp; GPU Constraints**: Camera APIs, biometric sensors (Face ID, Fingerprint), and GPU rendering engines behave differently on physical chipsets.
* **OS Version Fragmentation**: Testing simultaneously across Android 11 through 15 and iOS 16 through 18 ensures backward compatibility.

Sauce Labs provides an enterprise cloud of real, physical mobile devices hosted in secure data centers, enabling automated regression tests on every staging build.

---

## 2. Architecture at a Glance (The 2-Step Bitrise Workflow)

The integration splits into two distinct, governed steps within your Bitrise pipeline:

<DiagramExpand title="SAUCE LABS TWO-STEP PIPELINE ARCHITECTURE">

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph BuildPhase ["1. COMPILATION PHASE"]
        Clone["git-clone &bull; npm ci"] --> Compile["android-build or xcode-archive"]
        Compile --> ReadyBin["Compiled Binary Ready<br/>$BITRISE_APK_PATH or $BITRISE_IPA_PATH"]
    end

    subgraph Step1 ["2. STEP 1: SAUCE LABS APP CREATE"]
        ReqFile["Read saucelabs.request.yml<br/>from project root"] --> Register["Register App in Sauce Labs Storage API"]
        Register --> ExportIDs["Export Environment Variables:<br/>$SAUCE_APP_NAME &bull; $SAUCE_APP_ID &bull; $SAUCE_APP_FILE_NAME"]
    end

    subgraph Step2 ["3. STEP 2: SAUCE LABS UPLOAD AND TEST"]
        UploadBin["Upload Binary via Storage API<br/>https://api.us-west-1.saucelabs.com"] --> RunTest["Execute saucectl test_command<br/>Appium / Espresso / XCUITest"]
        RunTest --> StreamLogs["Stream Test Artifacts to Bitrise:<br/>Videos &bull; Screenshots &bull; HAR Network Logs"]
    end

    ReadyBin --> Step1
    ExportIDs --> Step2
```

</DiagramExpand>

---

