## 8. Troubleshooting Quick Reference

<div class="portal-table-wrap">
  <table class="portal-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Symptom</th>
        <th>Likely Root Cause</th>
        <th>Resolution</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>401 Unauthorized during upload</code></td>
        <td>Invalid or expired <code>$SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY</code> in Bitrise Secrets.</td>
        <td>Open Sauce Labs &gt; User Settings &gt; Access Key. Regenerate key and update Bitrise secret.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>App not found during test execution</code></td>
        <td>Upload step failed or <code>$SAUCE_APP_ID</code> was not passed correctly.</td>
        <td>Confirm upload step finished with HTTP 200 before test execution started.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Tests timeout waiting for a device</code></td>
        <td>Requested device model is unavailable or concurrency limit reached.</td>
        <td>Use wildcard regex (e.g. <code>Google Pixel.*</code>) instead of exact device IDs to pick available pool units.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>saucectl: command not found</code></td>
        <td>CLI runner not installed on the virtual machine stack.</td>
        <td>Add an install script step before testing: <code>curl -L https://saucelabs.github.io/saucectl/install | bash</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Wrong region error (HTTP 404)</code></td>
        <td><code>sauce_region</code> mismatch between Bitrise step and Sauce Labs account data center.</td>
        <td>Verify account data center (<code>us-west-1</code>, <code>us-east-4</code>, or <code>eu-central-1</code>) and align both configs.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

